What the parser emits. Shapes:
- `text`: printable characters in the current style (never contains control characters);
- `newline` (LF), `carriage-return` (CR), `backspace` (BS), `tab` (HT);
- `erase-line` with `mode` 0 = cursor to end, 1 = start to cursor, 2 = whole line (ESC[nK);
- `erase-display` with `mode` 0/1/2/3 (ESC[nJ; 2 and 3 clear the view);
- `cursor-home` (ESC[H / ESC[1;1H; a view only uses it to reset the column).

Input actions. Shapes:
- `set`: the native input changed (typing, paste, caret move);
- `history-prev` / `history-next`: ↑ / ↓;
- `submit`: Enter — records `value` in the history and empties the line;
- `reset`: Ctrl+C — drops the line without recording it.

Compile a filter or search string. `/expr/flags` is a regex (a broken one returns `{ok:false}`);
anything else is a substring, case-insensitive unless it holds an upper-case letter (smart case).
The empty string compiles to `regex: undefined`, meaning "match everything".

The streaming seam: anything that pushes log lines (a WebSocket, an SSE stream, `docker logs`,
a tail of a file through your backend). `subscribe` delivers batches and returns an unsubscribe;
`snapshot` (optional) hands over what was emitted before the subscription.

